{"cluster_id": "C-4449", "topic": "fsck's corrupted_runs finding was invisible on the", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-154"], "canonical_claim": "fsck's `corrupted_runs` finding was invisible on the fsck summary and treated as non-fatal even though it is a `clean()` term; separately the entry-gate fsck budget was inverted (subprocess timeout 180s vs scan deadline 600s), making the `--partial` degrade path unreachable from the harness, and 4 of 39 checkpoints in a 4h soak lost their whole fsck gate as a result.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/CURRENT.md#L529-L537"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4450", "topic": "Turning on fsck's --partial degrade path without", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-155"], "canonical_claim": "Turning on fsck's `--partial` degrade path without further changes would fabricate a consistency proof: a timed-out scan returns `dangling=0`, and the soak harness's `wait_for_pool_consistent` counts that fabricated zero as a clean read; the remaining `FsckTimeout` path still substitutes fabricated zeros and is tracked as BACKLOG `{#fsck-fabricated-clean-on-timeout}`, a landmine guarded today only because every consumer happens to check first.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/CURRENT.md#L538-L551"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4451", "topic": "D2 classified S31 (ca-gc-dryrun under gc_shards>1) as", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-166"], "canonical_claim": "D2 classified S31 (ca-gc-dryrun under gc_shards>1) as INFRA: `docker-compose-gc_shards2.yml up -d` returned rc=1 and the cluster never became healthy within 240s, producing 0/0 verdicts (errored at reset) rather than executing any test.", "issue_ids": ["S31"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-02-d2-scenario-triage.md#L12"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4452", "topic": "D2 found S21 (read-heavy many-ref) failed because", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-167"], "canonical_claim": "D2 found S21 (read-heavy many-ref) failed because the test ran `SELECT ... FINAL` against a plain `ReplicatedMergeTree`, producing `ILLEGAL_FINAL` on 12/48 queries, and separately its column-prune check (`1col=0 all=0`) was vacuous at dev scale because blobs were fully cached; recommended fix is to drop FINAL or use a ReplacingMergeTree and gate column-prune at a scale where blobs aren't fully cached.", "issue_ids": ["S21"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-02-d2-scenario-triage.md#L15"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4453", "topic": "D2 found S10 (patch parts + lightweight", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-169"], "canonical_claim": "D2 found S10 (patch parts + lightweight deletes) left a deleted bucket with 60 rows and patch parts observed = 0 (which may merge away quickly); classified as SCALE/TIMING, recommending verification at bigger scale with sync/settle before the count rather than treating it as a product bug.", "issue_ids": ["S10"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-02-d2-scenario-triage.md#L17"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4454", "topic": "The emulated S3-compatible backend (rustfs) answers TokenMismatch", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-218"], "canonical_claim": "The emulated S3-compatible backend (rustfs) answers `TokenMismatch` (HTTP 412) rather than `NotFound` for an `If-Match` DELETE issued against an already-absent object, so idempotent re-executions of a delete log as `outcome=replaced` instead of `absent`.", "issue_ids": ["P3-B1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/reviews-todo.md#L111-L134"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4455", "topic": "Plain-object CAS loops (casPutObject/casRemoveObject, used for namespace", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-296"], "canonical_claim": "Plain-object CAS loops (`casPutObject`/`casRemoveObject`, used for namespace files and mountpoint objects) run through the backend's default retry policy rather than `CasRequestController`, so they get no single-attempt client and no lease-relative deadline \u2014 bounded only by a local `MAX_CAS_ATTEMPTS=100` \u2014 meaning a flaky S3 could let such a write outlive the mount lease, the exact hazard the RFC timeout model forbids for the ref lane.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/02-store-core.md#9-weak-places"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4456", "topic": "The two CAS GC SQL verbs use", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-307"], "canonical_claim": "The two CAS GC SQL verbs use inconsistent naming: `SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GARBAGE COLLECTION` spells the phrase out while `SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC REBUILD` abbreviates it to `GC`, giving operators an inconsistent user-facing vocabulary.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/04-ops-mounts.md#5-1-sql-verbs-astsystemquery-type-text-enum-name-with-astsystemquery-cpp-20-46"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4457", "topic": "The ca-fsck entry gate timed out on", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-357", "B050-086"], "canonical_claim": "The `ca-fsck` entry gate timed out on a 5.5 GB pool (exceeded 180s) with `reachable=0` after 160s, meaning the scan had not finished its first phase; the timeout now degrades honestly to a logged skip, but the gate does not run exactly when the pool is large enough to matter. Additionally, Fsck's entry gate timed out on a 5.5 GB pool; an earlier observation reported `reachable=0` after 160 seconds without completing the first phase.", "issue_ids": ["#21"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/todo-20260726.md#L91-L96", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-26-list-incompleteness-investigation.md#L390-L394"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4458", "topic": "GC rebuild FORCE semantics", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B002-071", "B005-080", "B045-010"], "canonical_claim": "`FORCE` bypasses only the healthy-baseline refusal in `rebuildBaseline`; it does not bypass a competing leader or failed `gc/state` CAS. Additionally, A rebuild first health-checks the current state and refuses a healthy state unless `FORCE` is supplied; a broken or absent state proceeds through the recovery path. Additionally, Without `FORCE`, `SYSTEM CAS GC REBUILD` refuses to run when the existing `gc/state` and all referenced artifacts are present and decode successfully; `FORCE` deliberately overrides that healthy-state refusal.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/en/sql-reference/statements/system.md#L493-L495", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/04-ops-mounts.md#c-system-content-addressed-gc-rebuild-end-to-end-clickhouse-disks-ca-gc-rebuild", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#algorithm"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4459", "topic": "raw CAS subtree maintenance", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B002-100", "B035-066"], "canonical_claim": "A raw subtree deletion such as `rm roots/<server>/\u2026` is destructive offline maintenance and is not equivalent to `dropNamespace`, because it bypasses the journal and fenced index pruning. Additionally, `clickhouse-disks` exposes the logical `@cas@`-stripped view, whereas raw S3 listing exposes the physical archive; recursively removing a raw subtree is destructive maintenance and is not equivalent to `dropNamespace`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#path-mapping", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#blocking-gaps", "docs/superpowers/cas/CONSOLIDATION-COVERAGE.md#gap-fill"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4460", "topic": "The RustFS overwrite-leak workaround is a test-harness-only", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B002-109"], "canonical_claim": "The RustFS overwrite-leak workaround is a test-harness-only orphan reaper scoped to `roots/`; production CA code is unchanged.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/05-formats-and-backend.md#rustfs"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4461", "topic": "Read-only ContentAddressedMetadataStorage performs a check-only startup probe", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B003-057"], "canonical_claim": "Read-only `ContentAddressedMetadataStorage` performs a check-only startup probe, creates no GC or heartbeat thread, and throws a `READONLY` exception from mutating entry points.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#read-only-mode"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4462", "topic": "A legitimate CAS conditional-PUT collision can count", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B003-081"], "canonical_claim": "A legitimate CAS conditional-PUT collision can count as `S3_ERROR` or `PreconditionFailed` before being reclassified as `PutOutcome::PreconditionFailed`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/08-testing-and-soak.md#health-checklist"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4463", "topic": "The rebuild command surface is SYSTEM CONTENT", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B005-085"], "canonical_claim": "The rebuild command surface is `SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC REBUILD [FORCE] <disk>` and is logged through `CasGcScheduler` in `system.content_addressed_garbage_collection_log` with `gc_rebuild` audit events in `system.content_addressed_log`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#command-surface"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4464", "topic": "clickhouse-disks ca-gc-rebuild --disk <name> [--force] opens the", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B005-086", "B005-132"], "canonical_claim": "`clickhouse-disks ca-gc-rebuild --disk <name> [--force]` opens the disk read-only without claiming the server-root mount or creating a heartbeat, takes the independent GC lease, and exits nonzero on refusal.; The `clickhouse-disks ca-gc-rebuild` tool must use a read-only open, print rebuild counters one per line, print `refusal=<text>` on refusal, and never claim a live server's mount.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild.md#task-5-clickhouse-disks-ca-gc-rebuild--docs--memory", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#command-surface"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4465", "topic": "Rebuild refusal conditions are any missing or", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B005-087"], "canonical_claim": "Rebuild refusal conditions are any missing or invalid committed manifest body, undecodable ref shard, unreadable mount body, healthy current state without `FORCE`, or failure to acquire the GC lease.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild-design.md#refusal-conditions-fail-closed-diagnostic-report-always-produced"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4466", "topic": "The planned SQL rebuild surface converts performed", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B005-131"], "canonical_claim": "The planned SQL rebuild surface converts `performed == false` into `BAD_ARGUMENTS` with the refusal text, while also recording the refusal in the GC log.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-03-cas-gc-rebuild.md#task-4-system-content-addressed-gc-rebuild-force"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4467", "topic": "bounded S3-fault handling", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B007-053", "B018-016", "B038-059"], "canonical_claim": "Under S22's injected 503, 429, slow, and reset faults, 336 faults produced zero workload errors, replica agreement, and `dangling=0`; bounded retries absorbed the faults. Additionally, The planned S3-fault regression has a short-fault leg below lease TTL that must preserve the lease and a long-fault leg above lease TTL that must fence, back off, recover, and finish with `fsck` reporting `dangling=0`. Additionally, S22 requires bounded object-store `503`, `429`, slow-response, and connection-close faults to increase visible latency without data loss, unbounded retries, or committed partial refs.", "issue_ids": ["#37", "S22", "S30"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-16-cas-merge-upload-retry-fix-design.md#testing", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-06-scenario-validation-night.md#needs-infra-buildout", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/README.md#s22-object-store-throttling-and-retry-budget"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4468", "topic": "If gc/state is lost, attempt-local ref-base runs", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B010-087"], "canonical_claim": "If `gc/state` is lost, attempt-local ref-base runs are not independently authoritative; offline rebuild may conservatively union surviving runs and logs, may over-protect storage, and returns writable authority only after an explicit recovery action adopts a new baseline.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-10-cas-ref-snapshot-log-design.md#offline-rebuild"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4469", "topic": "If GC loses its cursor state, writer", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B011-121"], "canonical_claim": "If GC loses its cursor state, writer recovery remains valid because snapshots and logs are authoritative; destructive GC stays disabled until an explicit offline rebuild establishes a verified current-owner baseline.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#offline-recovery"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4470", "topic": "Any conditional-copy probe error or non-enforcing result", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B011-131"], "canonical_claim": "Any conditional-copy probe error or non-enforcing result selects local staging and logs that S3 staging is unavailable; it must never silently fall back to unconditional overwrite.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-s3-native-staging-design.md#capability"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4471", "topic": "Read-only retries are bounded by both attempt", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B012-083"], "canonical_claim": "Read-only retries are bounded by both attempt count and total wall-clock duration; exhausted budgets fail closed and defer the higher-level GC round or recovery attempt.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#bound-read-retries-too"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4472", "topic": "SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC REBUILD requires a", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B013-047"], "canonical_claim": "`SYSTEM CONTENT ADDRESSED GC REBUILD` requires a distinct `SYSTEM_CONTENT_ADDRESSED_GC_REBUILD` privilege and an explicit disk; omitting the disk is a syntax error and naming a non-content-addressed disk is `BAD_ARGUMENTS`.", "issue_ids": ["A\u00a79#8", "U#8"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L3029-L3146", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L153-L168"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4473", "topic": "drop-pool-member drain recovery", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B014-056", "B045-017", "B045-019"], "canonical_claim": "If any decommission drain step cannot confirm emptiness, the slot remains terminated with its farewell stamp, the report contains a warning, and a rerun is expected to complete the job; the operation reports blobs as `unreferenced`, never as `freed`. Additionally, Per-object drain failures during `SYSTEM CAS DROP POOL MEMBER` are recorded as warnings and leave the slot in a terminated-but-not-fully-drained state that a later invocation can resume, rather than raising an exception. Additionally, A non-empty `warnings` result from `SYSTEM CAS DROP POOL MEMBER` means some drain was not confirmed and the mount slot remains as a resume anchor.", "issue_ids": ["B200"], "sources": ["docs/en/sql-reference/statements/system.md#L524-L527", "docs/en/sql-reference/statements/system.md#L531-L532", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-pool-member-decommission-design.md#core"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4474", "topic": "Lowering materialization_grace_ms increases the risk that a", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B015-008"], "canonical_claim": "Lowering `materialization_grace_ms` increases the risk that a late-materializing predecessor write is dropped by the recovery seal and later reported as debris.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-13-cas-ref-lease-exclusivity-rev6-design.md#t-mat"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4475", "topic": "S39's long-fault assertions require a populated system.replication_queue.last_exception", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B018-026"], "canonical_claim": "S39's long-fault assertions require a populated `system.replication_queue.last_exception` and successful post-recovery writes before running an `fsck`-to-fixpoint check.", "issue_ids": ["#37"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-16-cas-merge-upload-retry-fix.md#L1537-L1699"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4476", "topic": "The MOVE-to-CA smoke contract is that disk_name", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B019-015"], "canonical_claim": "The MOVE-to-CA smoke contract is that `disk_name` changes `default \u2192 ca_smoke \u2192 default`, row checksums remain identical, and neither `Code: 236` nor a `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` exception occurs.", "issue_ids": ["S36"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca.md#L491-L541"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4477", "topic": "For other concurrent-read observations, CAS fsck is", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B026-039"], "canonical_claim": "For other concurrent-read observations, CAS fsck is designed to fail closed or report an inconclusive result: fresh reference checks treat a concurrently deleted blob or manifest as still referenced, checksum failures are catalogued as `CorruptedRun`, and timeouts set `partial=1`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-tool-read-without-ownership-design.md#safety-enumeration"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-4478", "topic": "The CI scrape is conditional on a", "target": "operations/troubleshooting", "member_ids": ["B026-044"], "canonical_claim": "The CI scrape is conditional on a failed functional-test result, and the stop operation is best-effort; therefore a force-claim liveness guard must be real even though the normal scrape is post-mortem.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-25-cas-gc-observability-and-mount-force-design.md#ci-scrape-check"]}

